MIT 8103 Advanced Database Systems
Real-time Game Leaderboard · Yomi Odukoya · Student ID 301907943
Project Title: Real-time Game Leaderboard Global Arcade Hub

1. Executive Summary & Organisation Selection
1.1 Organisation Overview
This operates an international network of physical arcade kiosks paired with competitive online multiplayer titles. 
The platform serves millions of active players globally, generating massive streams of real-time telemetry, transaction records
, and dynamic ranking updates.

1.2 Core Database Architecture & Objectives
To support the operational demands of the Real-time Game Leaderboard system, a Polyglot Persistence Architecture was designed and implemented:

Relational Layer (PostgreSQL): Serves as the immutable source of truth for core business logic, user profile management, player identity verification, financial microtransactions, and location metadata.

Document Store Layer (MongoDB Atlas): Serves as a high-throughput, horizontally scalable event stream engine for real-time score submissions, telemetry logging, and dynamic leaderboard aggregations.
2. Technical Architecture & Modular Portfolio Overview
The project repository is organized into five modular subdirectories adhering strictly to assessment specifications:

Module Summary
Table Module Core Deliverable Files Key Technical Achievements 
